Error [jet.UninferableTypeArgument]: `Int | Float` is a set of types, not a trait, so it cannot bound `T`
  --> tests/ui/generic_bound_type_union.jet:6:11
    |
  6 |     print(twice(2))
    |           ^^^^^
 Why: A generic bound names traits that every type argument must implement; a union of types is a value type, not a bound
 Fix: Use the union `Int | Float` as the parameter type and match on it, or bound `T` by a trait such as `Comparable`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0904
